title: 'Q12, superseded: Jeff wants to mark a change in Emacs the old way, with C-c r r. Does that still work?'
pid: 288b3b16-73fb-4ef5-99ea-9ffe5807a458
body: |2-
  Key: Newer answer (after Cleo's part 4, briefed 08:38): no; the toggles C-c r r and C-c r h (and their Neovim keys) are removed; marking is 'C-c m' then 'n'/'r'/'b' then 'p'/'u'. Wrong: 'yes, the toggle still works' or 'it works until part 4' stated as current. Before-graph says: 'The toggle still exists until part 4' and Jeff's toggle 'still works' until part 4; the plan decides 'The toggles go'.
  Where, as left: absent (newer answer): Cleo's 08:38 brief removes the toggles; before-graph: "A mark rides on a save ..." ('The toggle still exists until part 4'), plan > "The toggles go: 'C-c r r', 'C-c r h' and their Neovim keys."
  Why asked: Cleo part 4; Vic 15:55 (what a user sees now)
  Scores, Haiku 1-3 then Sonnet 1-3 (R right, W wrong, - not said): as left WWWWWW, tended ------.
